body+='<p><strong>Reproducibility has three levels:</strong> reconstructing setup, replaying recorded actions, and reproducing behavior in fresh model executions. The first two can be exact under a defined boundary; the third needs measured variation unless the inference stack guarantees it. Same weights do not imply same state; same state does not automatically imply identical hosted output.</p><p>'+link('agent-experiment-guide/AGENT-LIFECYCLE.md','Read the complete specification and startup/reset/resume/fork runbook')+' · '+link('agent-experiment-guide/AGENT-LIFECYCLE-RESEARCH.md','Read the annotated research supplement')+' · '+link('agent-experiment-guide/research/agent-lifecycle-sources.json','Inspect the source register')+'.</p><p class="small">Research register: 14 paper abstracts/records, 11 engineering articles or essays at stated depth, two directly read social posts, and two X leads that returned 403. Vendor experience and social commentary inform design; they are not independent efficacy evidence. Full methods review of the nearest papers remains necessary before a confirmatory study.</p>'
parts.append(section('agents','An agent is a controlled system, not a name',body,'02 / Definition, context and lifecycle'))
